# Agent-specific paths are generated by .sdlc/bin/link-agents.sh.
# AGENTS.md and skills/ are the single source of truth; these are just views onto them.
.claude/skills
.github/skills
.github/copilot-instructions.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build output. Anchored: an unanchored bin/ also matches .sdlc/bin.
/bin/

# Compiled test binaries. `go test -c` leaves these behind, and one was committed in
# feat-021 and carried for eleven increments: 14MB nobody noticed, because
# check-tracked.py only fails on a tracked file matching an ignore rule and there was
# no rule for it. The check is only ever as good as this file.
*.test
/canon

# Canon holds nothing. There was a database and a canon.yaml here; both went with
# cut-001, and the ignore rules for them outlived them by a month — a rule for an
# artefact the program cannot produce reads as though it still can.
#
# TestTheRepositoryHoldsNoStateOrConfiguration fails if either comes back, so this
# file is no longer the only thing standing between us and a committed database.

